{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516307-using-mythologies","id":1516307,"title":"Using Mythologies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-26T20:04:28-07:00","id":1516307,"title":"Using Mythologies","content":"Anyone have good stories of using the materials in Mythologies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-26T23:04:28-07:00","id":1516318,"title":"","content":"I never had the chance to do much with them outside of one-shots, but everything we did use (Mithras, mirrors) was pretty good. I remember even bringing the Mithras stuff to a RfR game, but ultimatly did not end playing that character (would mesh well with the group).<br /> I do remember playing around with torpor tethers but that was in a cross-over game with Geist. never finished it, but fond memories regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T08:48:23-07:00","id":1516345,"title":"","content":"Honestly, that book for me is the gift that keeps on giving.It is a great read indeed, full of interesting concepts that, even when not quite your cup of tea, can hit spots that will spark ideas of your own. Implementation could be a bit scattershot even for the time, but in a number of ways it can be considered as a sort of seed for the sort of setting hacks we would see in Wicked Dead &amp; Danse Macabre among other places. Those three are my favorite Requiem books ever, the ones I keep dragging them out of the shelves to mine for stuff to kitbash and rework in a variety of weird manners with all kinds of books and hooks. Still very much worth it even after all those years.<br /> <br /> <br /> For one, instead of picking between the two different takes on Torpor &amp; the Sleep of Ages presented in the book, i came the idea of keeping them as different layers of the same journey, so to speak, blending things with Awakening's Oneiros &amp; astral travel mechanics i would use to expand concepts.<br /> <br /> <br /> The Sleep of Reason or Surface Layer, also known as the Oneiros, is pretty much the same as the place described in MtAw and Astral Realms (based on many telling similarities with the &quot;Understanding the Fog of Eternity&quot; subchapter), what in practical terms means that through Torpor vampires may circumvent some of the requirements that Awakened deal with for astral journeys, up to the Oneiros at least, where some undead mystics have confronted what surprised Awakened might qualify as the soul's Daimon or entities akin to Goetic inner demons.<br /> <br /> All of this would also indirectly connect with dream-drinking from the &quot;Sleep of Reason&quot; chapter, the Alucinor and Usiri bloodlines, the Dream Visions merit from the Mekhet clanbook - and the Sightless Mother (more on that later).<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bBeyond that, things get a little turbid and less similar to what one of the awakened might expect from their &quot;inner dimensions&quot;, as below the self, impulses and urges of the Beast intrude and merge with the dark corners of a kindred identity past and present to form labyrinthine vistas at the same time alien and familiar to the dead predator once human that holds the ephemeral keys to the idiosyncratic landscape of these hedge mazes, endless caves of echoes and houses of phantasmagoric mirrors.<br /> <br /> (A sort of murky liminal space where one might lose itself in several sub-realms that bridge or cross over from part of the kindred self, beast and dimensions outside. Places like the Maze of Mirrors, where bits from the chapter on Red Jack &amp; the Mekhet clanbook's info on Hollows would bear fruit, Blood Mary and the Children of Thorns' personal share of Hedge landscape or other more obscure places like my whole homebrew realm of Yurema, might be found)<br /> <br /> <br /> And farther even lies only death - or more precisely, the place of the dead, the Thanatos Layer, the Second Death realm (mostly straight from Mythologies, with some Book of Dead bits peppered in), a place of broken hungry dead without bodies and fetterless ghosts, many all too ready to steal the tether/silver cord of those visitors who still have it for a chance at new unlife in a repossessed body so to speak, even though the Psychocomps that guard that place strongly frown upon it and may attempt to find cracks into the world of the living to try to recapture such escapees with bodies not their own.<br /> <br /> \u200bThough those Reapers who managed to find (un)auspicious circunstances (remember the the &quot;Blood Curses&quot; chapter?) to hack points of entry into our world after such body snatchers could all too frequently deviate from their initial objective to deal with other issues, like diablerists with their patchwork souls, or leave the emptied husk of a freshly spawned <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mnemovores\" target=\"_blank\">Mnemovore</a> or two when such stray soul captures were &quot;botched&quot; somehow.\u200b..<br /> <br /> <br /> So, for starters, i'd say that Mythologies has been a pretty big major part of fleshing out my own take of the whole &quot;other realms of existence&quot; gameplay that the other supernaturals seem to be so much into. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-27-2023, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T15:20:40-07:00","id":1517176,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1147_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1147\" data-vbnamecard=\"1147\">Baaldam</a> I always loved your interpretation for the the Mythologies part of Torpor as some sort of a eternally decaying level of the Astral, and have more or less headcanoned it","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-05T18:01:03-07:00","id":1517236,"title":"","content":"I really enjoyed reading Mythologies back in the day. The section on torpor has always grabbed my attention. Baaldam, I like your spin on the ideas and connections to other game lines!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}